  "about": {
   "heading": "How this model was made",
   "intro": [
    "Nothing here was drawn by eye from a single picture. The shape of the house comes from an airborne laser survey, its dimensions from the county's own record card, its colours and openings from photographs, and the ground from public elevation data. Each part of the model carries a note saying which of those it rests on - switch the display to Evidence and click anything to see.",
    "The roof planes were fitted to the 2017 LiDAR returns and the result was scored against every return that hit the roof. Wall positions follow the dimensioned sketch on the assessor's record card, registered to the surveyed eave lines. The exterior was renovated after the survey was flown, so cladding, trim and porch details follow the 2024 aerial photograph and the assessor's street photograph instead."
   ],
